\newpage
\item (2p) \textbf{Implementation (1p).} Implement the gradient bandit algorithm in \citet[Section~2.8]{sutton2020reinforcement}.

Use \texttt{gradient\_bandit\_algorithm(bandit, alpha)}. Initialize all $H_1(a) = 0$. After observing $R_t$, update the baseline to include the current reward:
\[
\bar R_t=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{s=1}^{t}R_s.
\]
Then update the preferences using $R_t-\bar R_t$ and the action probabilities used to select the current action. Recompute softmax probabilities afterwards. At the first step, $\bar R_1=R_1$, so the preference update is automatically zero. Return the same output structure as the greedy algorithm, replacing \texttt{Qt} with the final preferences \texttt{Ht} and action probabilities \texttt{pit}.
\textbf{Example (1p).} Include inputs, a call, seed and compact actual output from your implementation, with a brief explanation. Reuse a supplied example or the required experiments.

\examplebox{Updating action preferences}{
After the first reward of 1, the baseline is 1 and preferences remain zero, so each action has probability $0.2$. Suppose the second reward is 3 and $\alpha=0.1$. Update the baseline to $(1+3)/2=2$, giving an advantage of $3-2=1$:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Chosen action:}\quad H(a) &= 0+0.1(1)(1-0.2)=0.08,\\
\text{Each other action:}\quad H(a) &= 0-0.1(1)(0.2)=-0.02.
\end{aligned}
\]
Applying softmax makes the chosen action more likely.
}
\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}
<<gradient-example, eval=FALSE,size="footnotesize">>=
set.seed(4711)
gradient_bandit_algorithm(stationary_bandit, alpha = 0.1)
## $Ht
## [1] -0.09767824 -1.00460839 -1.83627818 -1.90776481  4.84632962
##
## $pit
## [1] 0.007038550 0.002841898 0.001237140 0.001151788 0.987730625
##
## $Nt
## [1]  99  21  15  17 848
##
## $R_bar
## [1] 1.902805
##
## $Rt
## [1]  1.7725176  2.3963182 -0.2864914 -0.3089120 ...

set.seed(4712)
gradient_bandit_algorithm(stationary_bandit, alpha = 0.1)
## $Ht
## [1] -1.155096 -1.255883 -1.273164 -1.913755  5.597897
##
## $pit
## [1] 0.0011629534 0.0010514564 0.0010334422 0.0005446043 0.9962075437
##
## $Nt
## [1]  10  29  24  21 916
##
## $R_bar
## [1] 1.883679
##
## $Rt
## [1]  0.62963402  0.94862700 -0.30089716  0.08850766 ...
@
\end{minipage}

\emph{Check:} \verb|mark_my_assignment(tasks = "gradient_bandit_algorithm")|

